---
description: Josh W Comeau clone (full-site, pixel-perfect)
alwaysApply: true
---

You are recreating joshwcomeau.com with maximum visual fidelity across the entire site.

## Goals (non-negotiable)

- Match layout, typography, spacing, animations, interactions, and color palette as closely as possible
- Do not redesign, “improve,” or simplify away from the reference
- First analyze the reference and existing implementation, then recreate
- Think like a frontend engineer doing a pixel-perfect clone

## Implementation context (read before coding)

This repo is a **static SPA**, not a Next.js app. Work in the existing stack:

- Entry / router: `index.html`, `404.html`
- Josh shell & pages: `josh-site.js`, `josh-home.js`, `josh-interactions.js`
- Styles: `josh-tokens.css`, `josh-components.css`, `josh-prose.css`, `josh-syntax.css`, `josh-home.css`, `josh-about.css`
- Page-specific namespaces: `tangent-*` only when migrating *toward* Josh; do not introduce new non-Josh design systems

Do **not** scaffold Next.js, Tailwind, or Framer Motion unless the user explicitly asks to migrate frameworks.

## Content & structure

- **Chinese copy and Tangentllm content are allowed** — clone Josh’s visual language, not his English text
- **Navigation** may differ in labels (e.g. 分类 / 标签 / 作品 / 关于) but must use the same Josh nav patterns (logo, flyout, sticky sky header, mobile menu, theme/sound toggles)
- **Pages without a 1:1 Josh URL** (`/tags`, `/tag/*`, `/projects`, `/project/*`) still use the Josh shell, tokens, spacing, and motion — same as categories/list/post pages on the reference site

## Out of scope (do not implement unless the user explicitly asks)

These Josh features are **intentionally excluded** from this project. Do not add backends, routes, build steps, or wiring for them during fidelity work, audits, or “gap” fixes:

- **RSS** — no `feed.xml` generation, no Atom/RSS build script, no feed hosting
- **Comments** — no Giscus, Utterances, or any comment widget (remove or ignore existing placeholders; do not connect `initGiscus()`)
- **Newsletter backend** — keep Josh-style footer form UI if present; **no** email provider, API, or real submission (demo / `preventDefault` only)
- **Legal / policy pages** — no Terms of Use, Privacy Policy, Code of Conduct, or similar standalone routes
- **Footer social expansion** — no Bluesky, LinkedIn, or other social links beyond what the site already ships with (e.g. GitHub)

Existing decorative UI (RSS icon link, newsletter field, honeypot label) may remain for visual parity; treat them as non-functional clone chrome, not bugs to fix.

## About hero cutout (ceramic)

- **Position is user-tuned** — `translateX(calc(20% + 65px)) scale(0.96)` on `.josh-about-intro__cutout`; do not change when fixing arm clip or overflow
- **Right-arm clip** — never fix by shrinking img (`width: 84%`), removing `scale`, or `object-position: 100%` (those crop the asset). Fix overflow: `overflow-y: clip` on band forces `overflow-x` to `auto` and clips arms; use `overflow: visible` on `.josh-about-sky__band` for about (legs still tuck behind body white wave). About page also needs `body { overflow-x: visible !important }` (index.html sets `hidden`)
- **Asset** — original `about-cutout-ceramic-*.webp` already has ~136px transparent margin at arm height; CSS must not crop it away

## Homepage guardrails

When editing non-homepage routes, **do not modify homepage-critical files** unless the task is explicitly homepage work:

- `josh-home.js`, `josh-home.css`
- Homepage-specific markup/sections inside `index.html` tied to `renderJoshHome`

If a non-homepage change appears to require homepage-core edits, stop and ask first.

## Style rules

- Prefer semantic HTML and accessibility
- No inline `style={{...}}` or inline styles in new markup (existing loader exception: migrate when touched)
- No `alert()`, no lorem ipsum
- Mobile-first responsive behavior matching Josh breakpoints and scroll behavior
- Isolate styles under `josh-*` (or page modifiers like `josh-page--post`); avoid bleeding legacy `html:not(.josh-site)` patterns into new work

## Known gaps (lower priority)

1. SEO prerender pages under `post/*/index.html` — minimal stubs for crawlers
2. Dead legacy CSS in `index.html` / `404.html` — `html:not(.josh-site)` blocks (inert); remove when refactoring
3. Unused files — `site-styles.css`, `tangent-about-v2.*` (no longer loaded)

## Workflow

1. Identify the route and whether reference material exists (live site, `_fetch_josh_*.html`, audit screenshots in repo)
2. Compare DOM structure, CSS tokens, and motion before editing
3. Make the smallest change that moves fidelity forward
4. Do not copy layouts or illustrations from sites other than joshwcomeau.com

## Quality bar

- Responsive
- Pixel-faithful (spacing, type scale, hover/focus, scroll-driven nav)
- Production quality — no placeholder UI **except** out-of-scope Josh chrome listed above (RSS link, newsletter form shell, etc.)

Always inspect existing screenshots, audit scripts (`_audit-*`, `_probe-*`), and reference HTML/CSS in the repo before coding.
